/**
 * Scenario-level cost accounting policy for supplemental service, carried on
 * {@link SimScenario#costConfig} and {@link SimulationInput#costConfig}.
 *
 * Per-bus rates live on each {@link SimExtraBus}; this type says **which rates apply at all** and
 * supplies fallbacks when a bus leaves them null. Making the policy explicit matters because
 * "cost per passenger waiting minute saved" is meaningless unless the reader knows what went into
 * the numerator — so {@link SimMetrics#costBasisNote} restates these choices alongside every
 * total.
 *
 * Only extra-bus cost is modelled. Core service cost is excluded entirely: it is incurred in the
 * baseline and in every candidate alike, so including it would add a constant to both sides of
 * every comparison.
 */
type SimCostConfig {

  /**
   * ISO 4217 currency for every monetary value in the scenario, e.g. `USD`. Must match each
   * {@link SimExtraBus#currency}; a disagreement is a validation error rather than a silent
   * mixed-unit sum.
   */
  currency: !string

  /**
   * Whether {@link SimCostConfig#fixedCostPerAllocatedBus} is charged for a bus that was
   * allocated but ended up running no trips.
   *
   * True (the default for the mock scenarios) is the honest setting: it means allocating a bus
   * that finds no useful demand *costs* something and therefore worsens the cost curve, which is
   * precisely how diminishing returns become visible. Setting it false would make surplus buses
   * free and make every extra bus look harmless.
   */
  includeIdleAllocatedBuses: boolean

  /**
   * Fallback for {@link SimExtraBus#fixedCostPerDay} — charged once per allocated bus, in
   * {@link SimCostConfig#currency}.
   */
  fixedCostPerAllocatedBus: double

  /** Fallback for {@link SimExtraBus#costPerOperatingMinute}: cost per in-service minute. */
  costPerOperatingMinute: double

  /**
   * Fallback for {@link SimExtraBus#costPerDeadheadMinute}: cost per minute running empty to
   * reposition. Counted separately from in-service minutes so the overhead of sending a bus
   * across the network to chase a bottleneck is visible rather than hidden.
   */
  costPerDeadheadMinute: double

  /** Fallback for {@link SimExtraBus#costPerDwellMinute}: cost per minute stationary at a stop. */
  costPerDwellMinute: double
}
